======================================================================
MUTATION A -- an app/api/session route handler in the app source
======================================================================

Claim under test:
  PASS  the export contains no server-side API route output

This mutation has two shapes, and they prove different things:
  A  -- a handler WITHOUT force-static: Next.js refuses it at BUILD
        time, so the export is never produced. This proves that the
        build rejects such a route; it does NOT exercise the
        export-tree assertion, because there is no export tree.
  A' -- a handler WITH force-static: the build SUCCEEDS and the
        handler is prerendered into the export as out/api/session.
        This is the shape that makes the export-tree assertion turn
        RED, and it is the one that proves the assertion works.

--- mutation: apps/studio/app/api/session/route.ts (no force-static) ---
export function GET() { return Response.json({ proxiedByNext: true }); }

